1) WHat is Docker ?
      Docker is a tool used to package an application along with all its dependencies ( libraries, configurations, runtime, etc.,) into a small unit called a container.
                                    or
      Docker is a containerization platform that allows developers to build, package and run applications consistently across different environments.


2) What is Container ?
      A container is a lightweight, isolated environment that packages an application along with all its dependencies and configuration, 
       allowing it to run consistently across different environments. Docker is the most commonly used container platform.


3) Diff bt Virtual Machinnes(VMs) Vs Containers
      Virtual Machine (VM)
      --------------------
            Plain Text
            Physical Server
            ↓
            Hypervisor
            ↓
            VM 1 (Guest OS + App)
            VM 2 (Guest OS + App)
            VM 3 (Guest OS + App)
            
            Each VM has its own Operating System.
            
      Containes
      ----------
            Plain Text
            Physical Server
            ↓
            Host OS
            ↓
            Docker Engine
            ↓
            Container 1 (App)
            Container 2 (App)
            Container 3 (App)
            
            Containers share the Host OS kernel.
            
      Difference
      -----------
          ===============================================================
         |   Virtual Machine	          |        Container              |
          ===============================================================
            Has its own OS	          |         Shares Host OS
            Heavyweight                 |  	Lightweight
            Starts in minutes	          |        Starts in seconds
            Uses more RAM & CPU	    |        Uses less RAM & CPU
            Larger size (GBs)	          |        Smaller size (MBs)
            Better isolation	          |        Good isolation
            Managed by Hypervisor       |     	Managed by Docker
          ===============================================================

      Real Example
      -------------
      Suppose you have:
            Spring Boot App
            MySQL
            React App
      
      Using VMs :-
            Plain Text
            VM 1 -> Ubuntu + Spring Boot
            VM 2 -> Ubuntu + MySQL
            VM 3 -> Ubuntu + React
          Three operating systems are running.
      
      Using Containers :-
            Plain Text
            Container 1 -> Spring Boot
            Container 2 -> MySQL
            Container 3 -> React
          All containers share the same OS kernel.

4) Docker Images and Registries

            Docker Images
            ------------
            A Docker Image is a lightweight, read-only template that contains application code, runtime, libraries, 
             dependencies, and configurations required to run an application. Docker uses an image to create one or more containers.
                                                or
                  A Docker Image is a read-only template that contains everything needed to run an application:
                  
                  Application code
                  Runtime (Java, Python, Node.js, etc.)
                  Libraries and dependencies
                  Configuration files
                  OS packages
                  
                  Think of it like a blueprint or template from which Docker creates containers.

            Registries
            ----------
            A Docker Registry is a centralized storage location where Docker images are stored, managed, and distributed. Images can be pushed to 
             and pulled from a registry. Docker Hub is the default public registry, while organizations may use private registries such as Azure Container Registry.
           
            =========================================================================
          |        Image                   vs             Registry                  |
            ========================================================================
            Contains application package	 |     Stores images
            Blueprint/Template             |	Warehouse/Store
            Used to create containers      |	Used to share images
            Created using docker build     | 	Accessed using docker push and docker pull
            =======================================================================
            
